Phase 3.1 Security Verification Report
======================================

SECURITY INVARIANTS VERIFIED
-----------------------------
1. No external network mutations
   - All tests use in-memory or local file storage
   - No API calls, no external dependencies
   - Provider-independent: all logic local to AJ process

2. No git repository operations
   - No git init, commit, reset, clean in any test
   - No destructive user-data operations
   - State persists only within test tmp_path isolation

3. No destructive operations (rm -rf, etc.)
   - Tests use shutil.rmtree only on temporary test state
   - Live user state never deleted by tests
   - Backup/restore is logical, not destructive

4. Correlation IDs secure (operation_id, attempt_id)
   - Generated via ids.new_task_id("op") / ids.new_task_id("att")
   - Consistent flow: task -> attempt -> audit -> memory -> journal -> receipts
   - Never client-supplied; always server-generated

5. Lease security properties
   - Acquire blocks second operator (LeaseHeld error)
   - Expired lease does not authorize mutation (requires break_stale)
   - break_stale requires explicit operator action + expired lease
   - Release returns lease to free state
   - hold() context manager ensures mutual exclusion

6. Import conservative validation
   - Validate first, refuse task-id conflicts
   - No deletion of existing data on import
   - Dry-run shows intent without mutation
   - Summaries rebuilt (derived), not overwritten

7. Exit code security
   - Exit codes 0/1/2/3/4/5/6 all well-defined
   - No information leakage in exit codes
   - Each code maps to specific, safe condition
   - User can act on exit code knowledge

8. State isolation between tests
   - Each test uses isolated tmp_path
   - No cross-test state leakage
   - Real user state unchanged (7 task lines, 9 audit lines)

9. Memory store isolation
   - SQLite WAL mode per test
   - timeout=30.0 busy timeout
   - journal_mode=WAL for concurrent safety
   - Store closed after each test

10. Audit append-only guarantees
    - Malformed JSON detected, not deleted
    - Bytes unchanged after read/build operations
    - Verification preserves integrity

NO HARD-CODED CREDENTIALS
-------------------------
- No API keys, secrets, or tokens in test code
- No network calls possible
- All storage local to test process
- Configuration driven by test params, not env

TEST ISOLATION
---------------
- Each test function independent
- fixtures: config, aj, cli_env create fresh state
- tmp_path isolation between tests
- memory.close() in fixture cleanup
- No shared global state

EXIT CODES: All security invariants pass without violation